  "notes": "Qwest/Elektra then Elektra/Atlantic adult-R&B soprano, 1998–2006. The research gives \"58–102 straight; ballads 58–80 with the backbeat on 3\", and five of the eight sourced tempos sit in the ballad band, so 58–80 felt with `halfTime` true is the base. Three drum deltas from \"restrained programmed kit, clap on 3 for ballads, 16th hats low in the mix\": a kick at one or two hits a bar with a 0.18 `beatSkipProb` — the entry names a guitar-and-clap-only bed, marked `[LOW-CONF]`, and a skipping kick is the nearest honest reading of it — a clap stacked on beat 3 with almost no ghost activity, and a continuous 16th hat held at a 0.2 main-velocity floor, a quarter of the parent's. Harmony is \"jazz-adjacent extended harmony with 4-chord cycles\", so every family is four deep and the triad share falls to 0.14. \"Light soprano placed high in the staff with controlled, small-interval melisma; harmony stacks thin (2–3 voices) to keep the lead exposed\" is a melody floor at MIDI 67 — the highest floor in the section — a 0.84 step share, and a countermelody density of only 0.26. ⚠ Confidence is **low**: the research rates the entry medium-low, says \"tempo spine sourced, harmony inferred\", and marks the key claim `[LOW-CONF]`, so the keys here are lane-level rather than named. ⚠ Every velocity, density and register number is INFERRED.",
